Feature Scaling Insight:
=>Feature scaling is an important preprocessing step in machine learning. It ensures that all features contribute equally to the model. In this assignment, both StandardScaler and MinMaxScaler were applied.
=>StandardScaler transforms the data so that the mean becomes 0 and the standard deviation becomes 1.
=>MinMaxScaler scales the data values between 0 and 1.
=>Scaling improves model performance and prevents features with larger values from dominating the learning process.

Correlation Analysis Insight:
=>The correlation heatmap helps identify relationships between variables in the dataset.
=>Positive correlation indicates that two variables increase together.
=>Negative correlation indicates that one variable increases while the other decreases.
=>Features with strong correlations may have significant influence on prediction.
=>The heatmap provides a better understanding of feature relationships and dataset patterns.

Bagging Insight:
Bagging (Bootstrap Aggregating) improves model stability and reduces variance by training multiple models on different random subsets of the dataset.
Advantages:
=>Reduces variance
=>Improves stability
=>Helps avoid overfitting
=>Works efficiently with decision tree models

Boosting Insight:
Boosting is an ensemble technique that builds models sequentially. Each new model focuses on correcting the errors made by the previous model.
Advantages:
=>Improves prediction accuracy
=>Converts weak learners into strong learners
=>Focuses on difficult observations

Model Comparison Insight:
=>Random Forest, Bagging, and Boosting models were trained and evaluated using accuracy score and classification report.
=>Random Forest performs well by combining multiple decision trees.
=>Bagging improves stability and reduces variance.
=>Boosting improves weak learners sequentially for better accuracy.
=>The model with the highest accuracy is considered the best performing model for this dataset.

